**Proposition 104.1 (general preparation and the marker alternative).**
For each source of Definition 103.1, Construction 62.3 supplies the
original general preparation of (103.1): build $u$ from one allocated
known-zero alpha, receive the owned target, use the terminal-control
right inverse, Hold and clear/isolate dependent records. With $I=N-b$,
its vector $(P,S,\mathrm{Read},\mathrm{Add},\mathrm{Tick},\mathrm{Hold})$ is

$$
\bigl(c,b-1,0,b(I+1),I,1\bigr).
\tag{104.1}
$$

There is also a different preparation on this same chosen family:
after constructing the zero field on $u$, actually Add $\theta_i$ at
the original beta marker $p_iL$ and $-\theta_i$ at $q_iL$, for each
$i$ including zero operands, then execute one old-graph Tick and Hold.
Receive and subsequently clear/isolate the owned input with the same
custody requirements. This marker preparation has vector

$$
\bigl(c,b-1,0,2k,1,1\bigr).
\tag{104.2}
$$

Both create $N-1$ cells beyond the initial alpha. Formula (104.2) is
the marker preparation, valid on both families below. It does not
change the vector or meaning of the original general preparation.
The alternative may receive exactly the same owned $N$-coordinate
target $x_\theta$ and extract $\theta_i=(x_\theta)_{p_i}$; its input
reception, target backing and extraction are paid too. It needs no
extra parameter oracle or changed receiver entrance.

**Proof of the alternative.** Before growth each beta marker has exactly
one neighbor, its owner. The source is still zero before the displayed
Adds, so its actual pre-Tick field is
$\sum_i\theta_i(e_{p_iL}-e_{q_iL})$. Applying the actual old adjacency
$A$ gives precisely (103.1), with all other coordinates zero. No
interior Add, hidden nonzero seed, inverse Tick or numerical assay was
used. Construction and complete binding updates are the existing
birth supplier; the owned-input reception and real removal of its
accessible copies are additional paid work. $\square$

